<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- Regression model for issue #67.  Written by BioNetGen 2.9.3 from
     tests/cpp/seed_build_model.bngl, then hand-edited in ONE place: the
     two seed species in <ListOfSpecies> list molecule P's components as
     (t, s, s) rather than in the molecule type's declaration order
     (s, s, t), and S2's bond moves with `t` to S2_M1_C1.

     That edit is the point of the model.  `init_species` resolves each
     seed species' component indices against the molecule type through
     `build_comp_mapping`, matching the N-th occurrence of a component
     NAME in the species to the N-th in the type; and BNG2's writeXML
     always emits seed-species components in declaration order, which
     makes that mapping the identity and leaves the whole path — and the
     bond endpoints resolved through it — untested by any generated XML.

     Regenerating this file from the .bngl therefore silently removes
     what it is here to check.  `seed_build_test` guards against that by
     asserting the seed species' names still list `t` first.  -->
